       IDENTIFICATION DIVISION.
       PROGRAM-ID. PB153RP.
      *> kb/Work PB153 - RESTRICTED DATA-POINTERS, END TO END.
      *> ANNEX D.9.2.2: "A RESTRICTED DATA-POINTER MAY CONTAIN ONLY
      *> THE PREDEFINED ADDRESS NULL OR THE ADDRESS OF A DATA ITEM OF
      *> A SPECIFIC TYPE", AND IT "PROVIDES TYPE SAFETY BY PRECLUDING
      *> THE TREATMENT OF DATA OF ONE TYPE AS DATA OF ANOTHER TYPE".
      *>
      *> THE DECLARATION SHAPE BELOW IS THE ONLY ONE THE STANDARD
      *> ADMITS, AND IT IS NOT THE OBVIOUS ONE. 13.18.60.3 SR18: "IF
      *> TYPE-NAME-1 IS SPECIFIED, THE TYPEDEF CLAUSE SHALL BE
      *> SPECIFIED FOR THE SUBJECT OF THE ENTRY" - SO THE RESTRICTED
      *> POINTER IS ITSELF A TYPE DECLARATION (PTR-T), REFERENCED BY
      *> A TYPE CLAUSE; '01 P USAGE POINTER TO TPT.' IS NONCONFORMING.
      *> 8.5.3.1 FORBIDS AN ELEMENTARY STRONG TYPEDEF, SO THE TARGET
      *> TYPE TPT MUST BE A GROUP.
      *>
      *> EXPECTED VALUES ARE DERIVED FROM 14.9.3.4 GR4a/b (ALLOCATE
      *> SETS THE RETURNING POINTER TO THE ADDRESS OF THE ALLOCATED
      *> STORAGE AND THE BASED ITEM'S IMPLICIT POINTER WITH IT) AND
      *> 14.9.3.4 GR6 (THE INITIALIZED PHRASE INITIALIZES AS IF BY
      *> INITIALIZE ... TO VALUE THEN TO DEFAULT - SO F IS 0), NOT
      *> FROM A RUN.
       DATA DIVISION.
       WORKING-STORAGE SECTION.
       01 TPT TYPEDEF STRONG.
          05 F PIC 9(4).
       01 PTR-T TYPEDEF USAGE POINTER TO TPT.
       01 V TYPE TPT BASED.
       01 P TYPE PTR-T.
      *> 14.9.3.3 SR4's ANTECEDENT IS NARROWER THAN SR5's AND THE
      *> DIFFERENCE MATTERS: SR5 SPEAKS OF A "STRONGLY-TYPED GROUP
      *> ITEM", BUT SR4 REQUIRES ONLY THAT DATA-NAME-1 "REFERENCE A
      *> TYPED DATA ITEM" - WHICH A WEAK TYPEDEF SATISFIES. THIS LEG
      *> IS THE OVER-REJECTION GUARD FOR THAT DISTINCTION.
       01 WKT TYPEDEF.
          05 G PIC 9(4).
       01 PTR-W TYPEDEF USAGE POINTER TO WKT.
       01 VW TYPE WKT BASED.
       01 PW TYPE PTR-W.
       PROCEDURE DIVISION.
       MAIN.
      *> 14.9.3.3 SR5 IS SATISFIED: THE RETURNING ITEM IS RESTRICTED
      *> TO TPT, THE TYPE OF THE STRONGLY-TYPED GROUP V.
           ALLOCATE V INITIALIZED RETURNING P
           DISPLAY "ALLOC=" F OF V
      *> 14.9.39.3 SR19: THE RECEIVER V IS STRONGLY TYPED, SO THE
      *> SENDER MUST BE A POINTER RESTRICTED TO TPT. P IS.
           SET ADDRESS OF V TO P
           MOVE 4242 TO F OF V
           DISPLAY "STORE=" F OF V
      *> 14.9.39.3 SR20: ADDRESS OF V IS A RESTRICTED DATA-POINTER OF
      *> TYPE TPT (8.4.3.11.4 GR2), SO THE RECEIVER MUST BE RESTRICTED
      *> TO TPT. P IS.
           SET P TO ADDRESS OF V
           DISPLAY "ROUND=" F OF V
      *> SR19's NULL LEG - "IDENTIFIER-6 SHALL BE THE PREDEFINED
      *> ADDRESS NULL OR ..." - IS PERMITTED WHATEVER THE RESTRICTION.
           SET ADDRESS OF V TO NULL
           DISPLAY "NULLED"
           ALLOCATE VW INITIALIZED RETURNING PW
           MOVE 77 TO G OF VW
           DISPLAY "WEAK=" G OF VW
           STOP RUN.
